Compact release analysis JSON follows as raw JSON:
{{ analysis_json }}

This is a post-publish fixup audit. The deterministic part of the
harness has already:

- Force-pushed `{{ release_branch }}` onto a fresh snapshot of
  `{{ base_branch }}`.
- Injected the shipped `## v{{ target_version }}` body verbatim above
  the next-older version heading.
- **Preserved `## Unreleased` as-is** — its entries describe work
  that landed AFTER `{{ fixup_tag }}` and so is NOT in the shipped
  binary. They belong in the next release, not this one.
- Skipped the audit, the publish dry-run, and the tag step.

Do one bounded evidence pass:

- `release_read CHANGELOG.md` — see both the v{{ target_version }}
  section and `## Unreleased`. Confirm v{{ target_version }} matches
  what shipped on `{{ fixup_tag }}` and that nothing in Unreleased
  obviously belongs inside v{{ target_version }}.
- `release_run` with `git log --oneline {{ fixup_tag }}..origin/{{ base_branch }}` —
  see what landed on `{{ base_branch }}` since the original publish so
  you can spot misclassified Unreleased entries (e.g., a doc fix that
  describes shipped v{{ target_version }} behavior).
- `release_search` on one representative Unreleased entry to confirm
  it describes work that was NOT yet shipped.

Return one short Audit block when finalization arrives. Do not produce
a draft changelog. If you find an Unreleased entry that should be in
v{{ target_version }}, flag it as a manual fix-up the operator should
move before the PR merges.
